## 1. Executive Summary

This report presents TLS configuration evidence and the results of the
project's A1 assessment. A1 evaluates negotiated TLS version, cipher suite,
certificate public-key algorithm, and certificate signature algorithm.

The classifications reflect the project's current assessment rules. They
are not a complete security audit, a comprehensive PQC readiness rating,
or a guarantee that an endpoint is secure.

| Metric | Count |
|:--|--:|
| Domains assessed | {{ findings.total_domains }} |
| Successful TLS scans | {{ findings.tls_successes }} |
| Failed TLS scans | {{ findings.tls_errors | length }} |
| A1 findings evaluated | {{ findings.total_findings }} |
| Acceptable findings | {{ findings.classification_counts.acceptable }} |
| Findings requiring review | {{ findings.classification_counts.acceptable_with_review }} |
| Unacceptable findings | {{ findings.classification_counts.unacceptable }} |
| Findings with unknown classification | {{ findings.classification_counts.unknown }} |

### Classification Guide

| Classification | Meaning |
|:--|:--|
| `acceptable` | Meets the project's current rule for this dimension. |
| `acceptable_with_review` | Requires further review or migration consideration. |
| `unacceptable` | Explicitly excluded by the current project policy. |
| `unknown` | Evidence is missing, unrecognized, or not covered by a current rule. |

Classifications apply to individual findings. A domain may receive different
classifications across the four A1 dimensions.

